{
  "version": 3,
  "note": [
    "The single source of truth for platform identity constants and for the",
    "transform a circuit applies before it hashes a value into a key. Solidity,",
    "Rust, TypeScript and Noir constants are generated from this file by",
    "scripts/regen-identity-handles.py. The transform is hand written in each",
    "language -- the circuit's is the one that keys a binding -- and Rust,",
    "TypeScript and Noir run the same vector table. Solidity only folds.",
    "",
    "The circuit checks that a value is exactly the JSON token the platform",
    "sent, nothing about its format: that is the platform's to keep. A handle,",
    "or an id that is a JSON string, is printable ASCII 0x20-0x7e without '\"'",
    "or '\\\\', so a commitment between revealed quotes holds one string. An id",
    "that is a number is decimal digits. A-Z in a handle fold to a-z; nothing",
    "else changes, nothing is trimmed, and an id is never folded. Each length",
    "is the circuit's buffer.",
    "",
    "A node is SHA256(tag || value): the handle node over the folded handle,",
    "the id node over the id exactly as the platform sent it. The tags are raw",
    "ASCII with no separator or length prefix, one per platform and kind, so no",
    "two platforms and no id and handle share a key. Every handleNode and",
    "idNode below was computed independently, with Python's hashlib over the",
    "hand-written output; the generator recomputes each one and refuses a",
    "table whose stored node disagrees.",
    "",
    "A platform id is keccak256 of the platform key ('x'), with no namespace",
    "of its own. The specification fixes the keys -- the launch profiles of",
    "REQ-PLAT-01 are google, x and github -- and leaves the derivation to",
    "the profile author, so this repository pins it."
  ],
  "platforms": [
    {
      "key": "x",
      "maxLength": 39,
      "note": "bearer-link's handle buffer, shared with GitHub.",
      "tags": {
        "userId": "libid.x.user-id",
        "handle": "libid.x.handle"
      },
      "id": {
        "maxLength": 20,
        "shape": "decimal",
        "note": "A decimal string; 2^64-1 has 20 digits."
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "github",
      "maxLength": 39,
      "note": "bearer-link's handle buffer: GitHub's 39-byte login.",
      "tags": {
        "userId": "libid.github.user-id",
        "handle": "libid.github.handle"
      },
      "id": {
        "maxLength": 20,
        "shape": "decimal",
        "note": "A bare JSON integer; 2^64-1 has 20 digits."
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "google",
      "maxLength": 62,
      "note": [
        "The address as proved: no dot is removed, no +tag stripped and no domain",
        "rewritten, so two addresses never become one identity. A longer one is",
        "refused, not truncated."
      ],
      "tags": {
        "userId": "libid.google.user-id",
        "handle": "libid.google.handle"
      },
      "id": {
        "maxLength": 31,
        "shape": "string",
        "note": "The OIDC sub, as the oidc-google circuit reads it."
      }
    }
  ],
